There are $d_1$ choices for each of the $k-1$ positions.
Thus, for a fixed length $k$ and fixed MSD $d_1$, there are $d_1^{k-1}$ Snake numbers.
Summing over all possible MSDs $d_1 \in \{1, \dots, 9\}$, the total number of Snake numbers of length $k$ is $\sum_{d_1=1}^9 d_1^{k-1}$.

